course: dictionary
lesson: 9113
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but have more than one meaning. Smelt is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which is its context. «how he smelt it on the road» Here smelt is the past form of smell: he noticed the smell with his nose.
explain: «Smelting heats the ore with a fuel such as charcoal or coke to free the metal.» The clues are ore, fuel and metal. Ore is rock with metal in it, so smelt means to heat the rock until the metal melts out.
explain: «The Leopard jumped at something that smelt like Zebra.» Here smelt is again the past of smell, because a thing can smell like something. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence, then try it in place of the hard word to check.
fact: Smelt is a verb with more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one is meant.
fact: In UK, Irish and Australian English, smelt is the past form of smell, as in «how he smelt it on the road». In US English people usually write smelled.
fact: Smelt can mean to heat rock until the metal in it melts out, which is called smelting.
fact: Smelting iron and copper in furnaces began the Iron Age and Bronze Age.
fact: Smelt can also be a noun meaning a small silver fish found in the sea and lakes.
exercise: «how he smelt it on the road» What does smelt mean here? | To cook food slowly | To heat rock until the metal melts out | *Noticed a smell, the past form of smell | A small silver fish
exercise: «Smelting heats the ore with a fuel such as charcoal or coke to free the metal.» What does smelting mean? | Sniffing a flower | *Heating rock to melt out the metal | Catching small fish in a net | Cooling hot metal quickly
exercise: Which meaning of smelt is a small silver fish found in the sea and lakes? | Gave off a loud noise | To heat rock until the metal melts out | *A small silver fish | Noticed a smell
test: «smelt like Zebra, and it felt like Zebra» What does smelt mean? | To shout loudly | A small fish | To melt rock for metal | *Past form of smell, meaning it had a smell
test: Which word is the usual US English form of the past of smell? | Smelts | *Smelled | Smelt | Smelting
exam: «Rocks with enough metal in them to be worth digging are called ores, and smelting heats the ore with a fuel.» Which meaning of smelt fits here? | *To heat rock until the metal melts out | Noticed a smell | A small silver fish | Smelly and damp
